//@ run-pass
//@ requires: madaros

// Adversarial proof that Task 5's dispatch is genuinely gated on the
// ACTUAL issuer key algorithm, not merely on the signature's hash OID:
// the real P-384-signed leaf from x509_chain_ecdsa_p384_signature.sio,
// verified against an UNRELATED P-256 root, must be rejected -- proving
// this is not "any EC key accepted for ecdsa-with-SHA384" but a genuine
// per-curve check with real curve arithmetic underneath. A P-256 public
// key run through the P-256 verification equation against an r/s pair
// produced by an unrelated P-384 signer over unrelated TBS bytes will not
// satisfy that equation, so `x509_verify_signature` must return `false`.
//
// LEAF_DER is byte-identical to the leaf fixture in
// tests/run-pass/x509_chain_ecdsa_p384_signature.sio (real openssl P-256
// leaf, ecdsa-with-SHA384-signed by a genuine P-384 root, independently
// confirmed via `openssl verify`).
//
// UNRELATED_P256_ROOT_DER is the self-signed P-256 root fixture already
// pinned in tests/run-pass/x509_chain_ecdsa_sha384_signature.sio (D15's
// own root_cert.pem/.der, `CN=sha384-root-test`) -- copied verbatim from
// that file's `root_der_bytes` constant. It shares no key material and no
// TBS content with the P-384 root/leaf pair above.

